1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,333
Phil [unspoken model note]: In the film, the ending is Phil playing piano. He hasn't tested this theory yet. The ballroom piano is free. This is the most direct test of his hypothesis.

2
00:00:10,333 --> 00:00:15,833
Town [stage]: Phil plays the last eight bars until he can get through them.

3
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:23,906
Larry: Taking the charge. Alma's got a girl in Pittsburgh and the place is going dark. You guys shoot the ballroom tonight, I'll be back.

4
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,833
Phil [unspoken model note]: At a table. In the ballroom. Among the party.

5
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:33,958
Town [stage]: Phil sits on the empty depot bench.

6
00:00:33,958 --> 00:00:38,958
Town [stage]: Rita goes dancing at the ballroom.

7
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:43,083
Town [stage]: Tuesday, February 2. Six am in the Hearthside Hotel.

8
00:00:43,083 --> 00:00:48,000
Town [stage]: Phil rides the coach and steps off at Pittsburgh.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,500
Town [stage]: Rita records Alma at the Rialto and puts her recording on the patch.

10
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:57,333
Town [stage]: Phil sleeps on the Pittsburgh terminal bench.

11
00:00:57,733 --> 00:01:04,853
Larry: Second take. She talked longer than the first. Charge died on the third word of the fourth sentence. You'll hear it.

12
00:01:05,817 --> 00:01:10,144
Rita: It's going to her. You don't have to say thank you. Go home, Alma.

13
00:01:10,708 --> 00:01:14,542
Town [stage]: Tuesday, February 2. Six am in the Hearthside Hotel.

14
00:01:14,542 --> 00:01:20,250
Town [stage]: I know that voice. Play it again.
